    "title": "Grace men, Saint Francis women keep rolling in doubleheader - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Ayen ,\n1 hours ago\nWINONA LAKE, Ind. (WANE) – No. 1 Grace men and No. 6 Saint Francis shined during Wednesday’s Crossroads League doubleheader at the Capital Center.\nIn the women’s game, Carroll High School grad Taylor Fordyce scored a career-high 31 points to lead Saint Francis (20-1) to a 95-80 win at Grace. The Cougars extended their winning streak to 11 games to improve to 10-1 in Crossroads League play.\nCrestview High School grad Cali Gregory finished with 20 points, adding four rebounds, an assist and a steal. Isabella Gizzi added 19, while Julia Mantyla scored 12 in the win.\nOn the men’s side, No. 1 Grace (21-0) remains unbeaten following an 85-74 win over Saint Francis. Manchester High School grad Gavin Betten dominated with a 21-point performance off the bench. Ian Raasch scored 17, Blackhawk Christian grad Gage Sefton added 15, while Hunter Walston and Grady Carpenter also finished in a double figures with 12 and 10 points, respectively.\nSaint Francis returns to the Hutzell Athletic Center to host Indiana Wesleyan for a men’s and women’s doubleheader on Saturday at 1 p.m. Grace visits Huntington for a doubleheader that also tips off at 1 p.m.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "6 Saint Francis shined during Wednesday’s Crossroads League doubleheader at the Capital Center. In the women’s game, Carroll High School grad Taylor Fordyce scored a career-high 31 points to lead Saint Francis (20-1) to a 95-80 win at Grace. The Cougars extended their winning streak to 11 games to improve to 10-1 in Crossroads League play. Crestview High School grad Cali Gregory finished with 20 points, adding four rebounds, an assist and a steal.",
